  "note": "Relay 5's coil feeds through its own N.C. contact (5F/5H, 5J) and buzzes whenever relay 6 is released, so powered phases with relay 6 out use fixed advances instead of settle. Light 5 hangs on 5J/6J/6H, not on relay 5's arm, so it stays lit through the buzz. The page states no observable for the set state ('The burglar alarm is now set'), so the pushbutton 1 presses carry no expect; light 5 OFF and relay 6 latched there are derived and left to Step 7.",
